1
00:00:00,287 --> 00:00:01,507
Cancer's strangest trick?

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:03,933
It starts with your own cells.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,830
Healthy cells follow signals:

4
00:00:06,996 --> 00:00:09,427
grow, repair damage, stop

5
00:00:09,442 --> 00:00:11,834
dividing. If damage is too

6
00:00:11,849 --> 00:00:13,325
severe, they can trigger their

7
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:14,360
own destruction.

8
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:16,272
But genetic changes can break

9
00:00:16,287 --> 00:00:17,400
these safeguards.

10
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,605
A damaged cell keeps copying

11
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,880
itself. One becomes two.

12
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,400
Two become four.

13
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:25,655
A growing mass can crowd out

14
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:26,600
healthy tissue.

15
00:00:26,772 --> 00:00:29,245
Your immune system can recognize

16
00:00:29,260 --> 00:00:31,160
and destroy abnormal cells.

17
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,589
But some cancer cells escape

18
00:00:33,604 --> 00:00:36,117
detection. Others send signals

19
00:00:36,132 --> 00:00:38,040
that switch immune attacks off.

20
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:40,215
Now the danger is growing behind

21
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:41,570
a convincing disguise.

22
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:44,015
And some cancer cells can break

23
00:00:44,030 --> 00:00:45,650
away and spread elsewhere.

24
00:00:45,806 --> 00:00:47,490
That's metastasis.

25
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:49,341
So how do you fight an enemy that

26
00:00:49,356 --> 00:00:50,282
looks like you?

27
00:00:50,423 --> 00:00:53,117
Immunotherapy can help the immune

28
00:00:53,132 --> 00:00:55,117
system recognize or attack

29
00:00:55,132 --> 00:00:57,628
cancer. Some treatments release

30
00:00:57,643 --> 00:00:59,243
the brakes on immune cells.

31
00:00:59,436 --> 00:01:01,416
It can work remarkably well for

32
00:01:01,431 --> 00:01:03,323
some people, but not everyone.

33
00:01:03,486 --> 00:01:06,048
Cancer is many diseases, with

34
00:01:06,063 --> 00:01:07,403
different vulnerabilities.

35
00:01:07,723 --> 00:01:08,985
The next breakthrough might

36
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,679
depend on a surprisingly simple

37
00:01:10,694 --> 00:01:11,353
question:

38
00:01:11,813 --> 00:01:13,701
how do we help the body see what

39
00:01:13,716 --> 00:01:14,643
it's been missing?
